==Russian==

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|orv|азъбукы|tr=azъbuky}}, {{borrowing|ru|cu|азъбоукꙑ|tr=azŭbuky}}, from the names of the first two letters of the Cyrillic alphabet, {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{compound|cu|азъ|боукꙑ|tr1=azъ|tr2=buky|nocat=1}}, a [[calque]] of {{etyl|grc|ru}} {{m|grc|ἀλφάβητος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|а́збука}}
* {{audio|Ru-а́збука.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|а́збука}}

# [[alphabet]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[а́збука Мо́рзе]]|Morse code|tr=ázbuka Mórzɛ}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[а́збука Бра́йля]]|Braille}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[слоговой|слоговая]] а́збука|syllabary}}
# ABC book, [[abecedary]]; [[primer]]
# [[ABC]] {{gloss|the rudiments of any subject}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|а́збука}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|alphabet}} {{l|ru|алфави́т}}
* {{sense|ABC book}} {{l|ru|буква́рь}}
* {{sense|the rudiments of any subject}} {{l|ru|основа|основы}}, {{l|ru|азы́}}

