==Ukrainian==

===Etymology===
Created in {{etyl|orv|uk}} following {{m|orv|азъбукы||tr=azъbuky}}, borrowed from {{etyl|cu|uk}} {{m|cu|азъбоукꙑ|tr=azŭbuky|sc=Cyrs}}, formed from the names of the first two letters in the [[Cyrillic alphabet]], {{m|cu|азъ||tr=azŭ|sc=Cyrs}} + {{m|cu|боукꙑ|tr=buky|sc=Cyrs}}, following the example of Greek {{m|el|ἀλφάβητος|}}.

Attested 1627, compare {{m|uk||язъбука|tr=jazъbuka|sc=Cyrl}} (17–18th century).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Uk-азбука.ogg|Audio|lang=uk}}
* {{IPA|[{{uk-pron|а́збука}}]|lang=uk}}

===Noun===
